From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:25:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winebus: Expose wired VitaPad as a DualShock 4 by default.

Prefer hidraw for VitaPad (054c:1337) and reuse the existing DS4 descriptor
and identity support without requiring a compatibility option. Honor the
existing DS4-v1 option when choosing the emulated generation.

Translate VitaPad's seven-byte USB input report into a complete DS4 USB
report, rather than only changing the PID. Preserve Square/Cross/Circle/
Triangle, L1/R1, Select/Start as Share/Options, rear-touch L2/R2 and L3/R3,
signed stick axes, and the eight D-pad directions. Opposite D-pad inputs
cancel. Digital triggers are exposed as fully released or fully pressed.

Initialize the cached input report to neutral and synthesize DS4
calibration, firmware and pairing feature reports. Keep gyro and touch
input inactive. Consume DS4 output and initialization requests locally:
VitaPad does not implement DS4 rumble, lights, motion or touch reports.

Keep the physical VID/PID internally for device matching. Use existing
hidraw/SDL deduplication, retaining the SDL fallback if hidraw cannot be
opened. Existing explicit backend selection and Steam Input filtering
remain authoritative. DS4 emulation needs host hidraw access; Proton
cannot grant device-node permissions.

Protocol credit: carlelieser's VitaPad v.2.0.0 firmware, corroborated by
deadbeef7's SDL mapping in issue #691:
https://github.com/carlelieser/vitapad/blob/v.2.0.0/skprx/main.c
https://github.com/carlelieser/vitapad/blob/v.2.0.0/skprx/usbDescriptors.h
https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/691#issuecomment-5340902900

Target the distributed v.2.0.0 layout. Unreleased upstream commit
d365eb3f780365af69437c7725c6c40b26ce0b45 changes face-button and D-pad bit
assignments without changing the USB identity, so that incompatible
layout cannot be distinguished by VID/PID and is not handled here.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
index c516d80..9ec7763 100644
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
@@ -1541,7 +1541,14 @@ static NTSTATUS hidraw_device_create(struct udev_device *dev, int fd, const char
         desc.is_gamepad = TRUE;
         TRACE("mapping Sony hidraw controller %04x:%04x to XInput.\n", desc.vid, desc.pid);
     }
-    if (!desc.is_gamepad && spoof_dualsense_as_dualshock4() && is_dualsense_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid))
+    if (is_vitapad_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid))
+    {
+        desc.spoof_dualshock4 = TRUE;
+        desc.spoof_dualshock4_v1 = spoof_dualshock4_v2_as_v1();
+        TRACE("exposing VitaPad %04x:%04x as DualShock 4 %s.\n",
+                desc.vid, desc.pid, desc.spoof_dualshock4_v1 ? "v1" : "v2");
+    }
+    else if (!desc.is_gamepad && spoof_dualsense_as_dualshock4() && is_dualsense_gamepad(desc.vid, desc.pid))
     {
         desc.spoof_dualshock4 = TRUE;
         desc.spoof_dualshock4_v1 = spoof_dualshock4_v2_as_v1();
diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
index 9ab4adf..e72306b 100644
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
@@ -1160,6 +1160,7 @@ static BOOL is_hidraw_enabled(WORD vid, WORD pid, const USAGE_AND_PAGE *usages,
     if (options.disable_sdl && options.disable_input) prefer_hidraw = TRUE;
     if (is_dualshock4_gamepad(vid, pid)) prefer_hidraw = TRUE;
     if (is_dualsense_gamepad(vid, pid)) prefer_hidraw = TRUE;
+    if (is_vitapad_gamepad(vid, pid)) prefer_hidraw = TRUE;
 
     switch (vid)
